WEBVTT

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:03.560
Nice to meet you, Shuta Aoi.

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:08.820
I am 0th, and I have returned
to set the 24th Ward right.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.990
So you're 0th, Ran's mentor?

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:12.530
OCTOBER 19, 2021

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:13.950
Are you Carneades?

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:18.740
No, I am not. Though, I am an acquaintance.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.790
That makes things easy.
Let me meet Carneades.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.960
I don't think
you would be granted an audience.

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:32.050
It may have nothing to do with you,
but for the past six months,

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:34.430
Carneades has totally been toying with me.

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:35.300
Besides,

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:39.560
it has something to do with my childhood friend
who's supposed to be dead.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:43.350
A strange tale.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:47.560
Fair enough.

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:52.940
Carneades is currently
at the highest floor of the Cornucopia.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:54.950
Why in such a...

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:58.660
<i>Is he going to make us choose another future?</i>

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:00.240
A storm is approaching.

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:04.210
What's your relationship with Carneades?

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:08.040
You should head over quickly,
or you may miss your chance.

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:09.630
Damn it.

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:10.630
Whoa, whoa.

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:13.300
That's right, can you tell me
your contact information?

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:15.420
You can ask Ran later.

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:19.430
And Ran isn't answering the phone right now
because the SARG is after him.

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:24.850
Oh, fine. It's only contact info.

00:02:57.940 --> 00:03:00.030
It's pouring.

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:02.410
Where did Shuta go?

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:03.820
Who knows?

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:07.580
Sheesh, he bailed on cleanup.
What the heck is he doing?

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:09.620
- Shu!
- Shuta!

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:11.210
Mari, take this.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:12.880
Whoa!

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:21.340
You're too fast.

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:24.350
Just like Tsuzuragawa said,

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:28.720
the smart city concept created by Mother
was the basic theory for the KANAE System.

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:32.900
Additionally, this theory
was scrapped by Mother herself.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:35.480
Asumi.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:39.440
Shu, you don't want to answer your phone?

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:40.950
ASUMI

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:43.530
From Asumi?

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.660
This means that...

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:46.700
Yeah.

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:49.410
<i>Asumi. Carneades.</i>

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.660
<i>My head is getting all jumbled up.</i>

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.330
At the top of the Cornucopia...

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:33.080
control will be lost from cranes
after a lightning strike and will collapse.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:38.040
The fall of tower cranes
will create many casualties.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:49.050
The only person who can stop this
is the one person atop the tower.

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:52.060
However, right after connecting the cables,

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:58.810
that person will be struck by lightning and die.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:04.650
If you warn that person of the lightning strike
with a direct call from the command room,

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:07.570
that person's life will be spared.

00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:12.910
Will you let the cranes fall
and sacrifice many people,

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.830
or will you sacrifice the one person
on top of the tower?

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:18.880
Guide the future.

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:24.920
Sh-Shu?

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:29.010
<i>Wasn't it Carneades
who was giving out the trolley dilemmas?</i>

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:31.470
Shu? What's wrong?
Was the phone call really from Asumi?

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:31.930
<i>Why am I seeing a future
where he becomes the victim?</i>

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:34.230
I don't get it.

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:38.730
- Like I would get any of this!
- Shu!

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:42.980
<i>I'll just ask him in person.
That should solve everything.</i>

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:46.570
Sheesh. Now of all times...

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:50.070
But now, I can...

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:52.580
Instructor.

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:54.290
OCTOBER 17, 2021

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:56.160
So it really was you
who instigated the Graffiti War.

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:59.710
You've become good
at drawing art that sends messages.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:01.960
Why'd you do that to Mr. Kaba's art?

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:04.670
Those really were some of my masterpieces.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:10.300
Because it was a masterpiece with so much
emotion packed in, it was worth overwriting.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:15.520
Its value rises because it's now gone,
and the agitative effect increases.

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:17.270
But that piece—

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:19.600
Do you have the right to get angry?

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:29.570
Indeed, I used the fame of Carneades
to overwrite graffiti and stirred people's anger.

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:35.540
I hired internet media to instigate conflict
with the "Graffiti War" article.

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:39.960
And they have no idea that trouble
is created by the one who resolves it.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:44.630
DoRed has more enemies now,
but gained many more followers.

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:47.460
Donations coming in now
are beyond comparison to before.

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:53.850
You used Carneades
for your own activities as well. Am I mistaken?

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:58.890
And when the artist Carneades fades out,

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:02.400
we can head into the referendum
while the topic is really hot.

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:06.110
Listen up. The KANAE System
is a double-edged sword.

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:09.650
It's highly convenient,
but also filled with danger.

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:15.410
The KANAE System is something that can destroy
the humanity that makes humans human.

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:20.080
There will no longer be a place for the weak?
The story is on a completely different level.

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:25.670
That system is technology that steps into a realm
that should not be trespassed as humans.

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:28.460
What are the laurels they rest upon?

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:33.970
Ran, you said that "your powers are enhanced"
when Asumi calls you.

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:38.270
That technology is an adaptation of military tech
at the foundation of the KANAE System.

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:40.430
It's called "cipher."

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:41.480
Cipher?

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:46.070
It shares its technological roots
with Kunai's Di-VA and Drug D.

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:50.240
We don't have time left before the referendum.
Art simply won't be enough.

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:53.950
We need to caress the physical body
of the 24th Ward simultaneously with its heart.

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:58.450
I have one favor to ask.
It's something only you can do.

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:01.040
What are you going to make me do?

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:06.960
I want you to hack into
the KANAE System database.

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:10.970
OCTOBER 19, 2021

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:13.220
You say that like it's really easy.

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:16.470
I'm nothing more than an ally of the weak.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:21.020
<i>That should be what Asumin wished for, too.</i>

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:24.350
Tsuzuragawa,
get away from there immediately.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:28.570
Listen up. We'll lose control of tower cranes
from a lightning strike and they'll fall down.

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:30.860
<i>I see.</i>

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:32.240
H-Hey.

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:33.740
Tsuzuragawa!

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:36.780
I'm back.

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:37.910
Welcome back.

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:40.370
Oh, our poster girl has come home.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:43.500
There's been rumors
that you married the guy next door.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:47.710
That's right. I haven't seen you at all
so this old man has been sad.

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:47.710
Huh? What's with that?

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:49.880
Small communities are so scary.

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:52.420
So how is it between you and Shu, anyway?

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:53.840
No ifs, ands, or buts.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:56.510
Shu is such...

00:08:57.220 --> 00:08:58.760
an idiot.

00:08:57.220 --> 00:08:59.850
Postpone it!
We're postponing any further work.

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:03.270
Are there any direct phone lines to the top?

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:08.900
Lightning warning?

00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:16.570
Ran?

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:17.910
You were here.

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:18.950
Look at this.

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:21.740
Carneades.

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:23.160
Probably the real one.

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:29.420
I have no idea what kind of contraption this is,

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:33.380
but if he'll stop the crane from
getting out of control, I have no complaints.

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:34.760
Stop it.

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:38.760
You might be thinking
that heroes save everyone,

00:09:39.010 --> 00:09:41.760
but you really need to start choosing, Shu.

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:45.390
I'll choose the future
where the crane doesn't topple over.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:47.310
Of course, I'm going to evacuate people too.

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:50.610
I won't choose a future that's already decided.

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:52.820
I'll save Carneades as well.

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:56.610
And I'll ask why he's doing this,
even if I have to punch him.

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:58.660
I wouldn't be satisfied otherwise.

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:12.630
Answer. Come on, pick up the phone. Hurry up.

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:14.710
Why?

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:16.050
Why!

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:22.100
The Vision showed us that a direct phone call
would switch the rails of the trolley.

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:24.560
But why isn't he answering the phone?

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:27.480
No, I'll worry about that later.

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:29.900
I have my own job to fulfill.

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:35.940
Koki. You too?

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:40.110
You want to say choose the future,
and save more people, right?

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:44.370
No way. I'm going to be a hero
who'll never give up on anything.

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:46.700
I promised that with Asumi.

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:00.260
Koki?

00:11:03.430 --> 00:11:06.220
<i>Fire alert. This is a fire alert.</i>

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:11.980
<i>Everyone inside the Inner Section,
please immediately evacuate to the Outer Section.</i>

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:17.860
<i>All security guards, please move to the Outer Section
immediately after guiding everyone else.</i>

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:20.990
<i>I repeat, this is a fire alert.</i>

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:26.700
<i>No system is left without holes,
but Cornucopia's system is close to perfect.</i>

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:30.000
<i>If there's any moment I can dive in,
it would be now.</i>

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:34.040
<i>It's at this moment,
while my abilities are boosted.</i>

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:41.430
<i>Ran, we're good to go anytime.</i>

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:43.090
We'll proceed with the plan.

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:45.350
<i>Yamamori,
you secure shelter and transportation.</i>

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:47.890
<i>Lucky, you create a diversion
with a fabricated fire.</i>

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:49.230
I copy.

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:53.190
I'm gonna do a really sloppy job,
so you'll have to clean up after me.

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:55.770
Oh no, that's so scary.

00:11:57.900 --> 00:12:01.030
All right, I'll head over as backup.

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:03.360
Something happen?

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:06.740
Apparently there's a fire
right in front of this building.

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:09.080
I'm going to go help guide the evacuees.

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:10.080
Got it.

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:14.540
Are you hesitating?

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:18.300
This is on a different level than just graffiti.

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:20.840
It's a crime I can't make excuses for.

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:24.050
Even if it's to save Shantytown...

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:27.180
<i>I wonder if Asumin would forgive me.</i>

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:31.390
That kindness is what killed Kunai.

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:42.110
I better make it in time.

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:10.970
<i>The tower cranes have electronic controls
to prevent accidents</i>

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:13.890
<i>but that's now malfunctioning
from that lightning strike.</i>

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:19.650
<i>If things go exactly like that Vision, the cranes
will topple unless we switch the cables.</i>

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:26.110
Sheesh, one-way communication security
is so freaking troublesome.

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:30.580
But if I've come this far,
it's as good as mine now.

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:32.830
So, let's do this.

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:36.420
I'll show you what kind of determination
little ol' me has.

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:44.130
<i>Ms. Tsuzuragawa. Nothing less from her.</i>

00:13:44.130 --> 00:13:46.430
<i>She does a good job at hiding the contents.</i>

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:49.970
<i>But...</i>

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:58.270
<i>Right now, little ol' me
can even rewrite the laws of physics.</i>

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:07.740
Records of various sensors,
social media history...

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:10.780
It's a hodgepodge
of all sorts of accumulated data.

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:12.950
Is this worth stealing at all?

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:18.420
<i>So that's what this is about?</i>

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:24.050
<i>Yeah, if they want to win
the referendum, this would be...</i>

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:34.720
Carneades.

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:41.900
Run for it!

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:44.940
The lightning!

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:04.340
Hey, Carneades. Get a hold of yourself!

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:05.800
Carne...

00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:13.720
Are you serious?

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:26.650
I'm sorry, Tsuzuragawa.

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:30.450
The KANAE System is in trouble.

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:34.620
I may not be able
to protect Miss Asumi's secret.

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:36.580
You can't protect Asumi?

00:15:36.990 --> 00:15:38.160
That means...

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:40.080
I will disclose it to you now.

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:42.710
The true identity of Carneades is me.

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:46.130
I'm more than slightly disturbed.

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:48.510
But that all makes sense now.

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:51.300
What is your objective?

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:53.890
The KANAE System has a critical bug.

00:15:53.890 --> 00:15:57.010
I cannot allow Mr. Gori to find out about it.

00:15:57.140 --> 00:16:00.430
That is why I played the role of Carneades.

00:16:00.980 --> 00:16:06.360
I mislead him, saying that the bug
was a result of Carneades's hacking.

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:10.860
Wait. Then perhaps those futures
that were shown to us...

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:15.410
So you've all been shown futures.

00:16:15.740 --> 00:16:19.750
I had speculated as such from the logs,
but I'm reassured that they were correct.

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:22.540
I named those events "Visions."

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:26.500
"Vision." That's a good, straightforward name.

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:28.800
About those Visions...

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:32.510
Of course, they aren't limited to the two choices
that Carneades created.

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:36.510
Those are the nightmares the KANAE System
had suffered as a result.

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:39.010
Just as I thought. Then, Asumi is...

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:44.230
Yes. Miss Asumi's consciousness
still remains in the KANAE System.

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:47.770
That means...

00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:52.030
Asumi is still alive?

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:55.160
I don't know what conclusion to make.

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:59.030
However, Mr. Gori decided to donate
Miss Asumi's physical body

00:16:59.290 --> 00:17:04.580
as a part of the KANAE System
because Miss Asumi was already deceased.

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:07.630
He felt overwhelming sorrow doing so.

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:14.380
If Mr. Gori ever finds about this fact,
he may as well go insane.

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:18.180
<i>I'm the one who pulled the trolley's lever.</i>

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:21.930
<i>Tsuzuragawa knows about
the existence of the Visions.</i>

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:27.690
<i>Because of my careless phone call,
she understood that she was riding atop the rails,</i>

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:29.690
<i>and decided to sacrifice herself.</i>

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:33.860
<i>I killed Tsuzuragawa.</i>

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:37.070
This program...

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:39.410
I will share this with you just in case.

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:42.830
After all, I don't know when
you will have your next Vision.

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:51.630
Tsuzuragawa,
I will continue on with your wishes.

00:17:56.220 --> 00:17:58.260
<i>Choose your future.</i>

00:17:58.430 --> 00:18:00.640
<i>Choose your future.</i>

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:03.180
<i>My name is Carneades.</i>

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:09.730
Information is more actively moving around.

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:11.940
Did Carneades show himself?

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:14.940
I have to hurry out of here
or it'll get dangerous.

00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:17.110
Give me a break. Hey!

00:18:17.110 --> 00:18:19.450
Come on. Why?
What's going on here?

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:22.620
I don't get it. I don't get it at all.

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:24.750
You can't just die like this.

00:18:24.750 --> 00:18:29.170
I won't allow for such a half-baked ending.

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:38.430
The cable...

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:45.520
Impossible.

00:18:45.980 --> 00:18:48.940
Tsuzuragawa risked her life
to stop it from going out of control.

00:18:49.690 --> 00:18:51.940
Did Shuta do something he didn't need to do?

00:18:52.150 --> 00:18:53.770
I'm not done yet.

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:56.990
Don't give up. Don't give up, me!

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:59.410
Ms. Tsuzuragawa is still alive.

00:18:59.410 --> 00:19:02.780
I'll... save... everything.

00:19:02.780 --> 00:19:06.080
I... promised... Asumi that.

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:08.910
That's what a hero is.

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:12.330
That's who I really... want to become.

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:15.880
So this time for sure... I beg of you, God.

00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:19.090
Ms. Tsuzuragawa!

00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:25.970
What?

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:34.690
Brother?

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:35.980
Ran.

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:38.740
Shuta.

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:49.710
Crap. What the hell is this?

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:52.710
<i>Help me.</i>

00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:01.090
Asumin?

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:05.050
The KANAE System.

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:31.830
An ambulance!
Someone call for an ambulance!

00:20:37.090 --> 00:20:39.670
OCTOBER 20, 2021

00:20:54.560 --> 00:20:55.810
Thank you...

00:20:56.730 --> 00:20:58.730
for saving Satchan.

00:21:00.480 --> 00:21:04.610
I'm sorry for poking fun
at all your hero work stuff.

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:10.290
I'm not a hero until Ms. Tsuzuragawa
regains consciousness.

00:21:11.660 --> 00:21:12.790
I see.

00:21:14.420 --> 00:21:16.130
Damages to the KANAE System?

00:21:16.380 --> 00:21:18.460
Fortunately, not much.

00:21:18.590 --> 00:21:20.000
What about Tsuzuragawa?

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:22.460
She still hasn't come to.

00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:24.760
We don't have any time left
until the referendum.

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:27.010
I'm counting on you
to lead the recovery efforts.

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:33.350
And about Carneades.
I can't leave him running free.

00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:36.560
I don't care how you do it.
Capture him at any cost.

00:21:37.400 --> 00:21:42.900
Mother at one point gave up plans for Cornucopia
and strived to become an educator, right?

00:21:43.320 --> 00:21:44.990
What about it?

00:21:45.400 --> 00:21:49.160
Would Mother be happy about
how the 24th Ward is now?

00:21:53.450 --> 00:21:55.000
A foolish question.

00:21:56.330 --> 00:21:57.920
Looks like things went well?

00:21:58.540 --> 00:22:00.750
What are you going to use that data for?

00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:04.880
I will use this data to hack into the 24th Ward

00:22:06.050 --> 00:22:09.010
and destroy the KANAE System.

00:22:09.680 --> 00:22:13.930
Instructor, you were in the same laboratory
as Ms. Kanae, right?

00:22:14.390 --> 00:22:16.390
If you know, can you tell me?

00:22:16.940 --> 00:22:18.980
What's inside that thing?

00:22:19.610 --> 00:22:22.020
What the hell is the KANAE System, anyway?

00:22:23.530 --> 00:22:26.030
It's a demon...

00:22:27.150 --> 00:22:28.740
that destroyed my world.
